# Test-Driven Development

Adapted from https://github.com/addyosmani/agent-skills (test-driven-development).

Write a failing test before the code that makes it pass. Tests are proof — "seems right" is
not done.

**Cycle:** RED (write a test that fails) → GREEN (minimum code to pass) → REFACTOR (clean up,
tests stay green). Run tests after each step.

**Prove-It pattern (bug fixes):** don't start by fixing. First write a test that reproduces the
bug and fails, then implement the fix until it passes, then run the full suite.

**In this repo:**
- Use `pytest`; test `core/` logic against real `nifty_data/` fixtures (incl. empty `{}` files).
- Cover happy path + at least one edge case per unit.
- Pure-logic tests need no DB; mock `core.db` or use a throwaway DB for write paths.
- Skip TDD only for pure config/docs/static changes with no behavioral impact.
